 # Account Legacy Card
 
-A lightweight RuneLite plugin that displays a concise account summary card when you log in.
+Account Legacy Card is a lightweight RuneLite external plugin that posts a concise account snapshot to the in-game chat when you log in. It is intentionally local-only: the plugin reads the active RuneLite client state and does not call Wise Old Man, TempleOSRS, or any other external API.
 
 ## Features
 
-- Shows player name, total level, and combat level in chat on login
-- No external API calls - uses only local RuneLite client data
-- Configurable via the standard RuneLite config panel
+- Displays the local player name, total level, and combat level in a single login message.
+- Handles missing player data gracefully while the client is still settling after login.
+- Optional reminder text explaining that the card is a local RuneLite snapshot.
+- No background jobs, network requests, credentials, or persisted account history.
 
-## Installation
+## Configuration
 
-### Development Setup
+The plugin appears in RuneLite as **Account Legacy Card**.
 
-1. Ensure you have Java 11 installed (`JAVA_HOME=/opt/data/jdks/current-java11`)
-2. Clone this repository and navigate into it
-3. Run `./gradlew build` to compile and package the plugin
+| Setting | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Show on login | On | Sends the account card to chat each time RuneLite reaches `LOGGED_IN`. |
+| Include reminder | On | Adds `Local RuneLite snapshot; no external API calls.` to the message. |
 
-### Running in RuneLite
+Example chat output:
 
-1. Build the plugin: `./gradlew assemble`
-2. The resulting JAR will be in `build/libs/`
-3. Add the JAR to RuneLite's `plugins` folder or use `--plugin-path`
-
